{
  "description": "Environment variable names read by the Go binary and host launcher. Every key has a category (INV-ENV-04): secret, user_endpoint, host, or violation. A violation is platform configuration that still arrives through the environment; that set may only shrink (see internal/constants/env_vars_registry_test.go).",
  "categories": {
    "secret": "API keys, tokens, client secrets, encryption keys",
    "user_endpoint": "User-specific endpoint or identity with no correct universal default",
    "host": "Host fact provided by the OS, read as a fact rather than as g8e configuration",
    "violation": "Platform configuration or test switch read from the environment; scheduled for removal in the env-config-purge follow-on"
  },
